;;
;; REPL/RedTeam/[RT-B]_PermissionlessReach.repl — FAMILY B: permissionless reach.
;;
;; "What is reachable with no capability, and what is reachable while SKIPPING Talos — and
;;  therefore skipping billing?"
;;
;; The second half is the one specific to this architecture. CLAUDE.md states two rules without
;; qualification: Talos is "the only supported client path", and it is "the only place IGNIS is
;; collected after a C_". Any path that reaches a state change without passing through Talos is an
;; operation nobody paid for, and it is invisible to every cost measurement in the suite — all 397
;; of which measure a Talos call.
;;
;; Run: cd REPL && pact "RedTeam/[RT-B]_PermissionlessReach.repl"
;;
(load "../deploy-stage00.repl")
(load "../deploy-stage01.repl")

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-B-001 - reach a sovereign admin op without Talos, and pay nothing")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-B-001 · 01 · the master key satisfies the inter-module gate ====
(print "--- [RT-B-001 · 01 · the master key satisfies the inter-module gate] ---")
;;<<RT-B-001>> FAMILY: B | STATUS: FIXED
;;HYPOTHESIS: `P|UEV_IMC` is described as an INTER-MODULE gate -- it should pass only for a caller
;;            that IS a registered module, which is what makes "Talos is the only supported client
;;            path" true. But the genesis sequence registers the MASTER KEYSET itself as a DALOS
;;            policy. If that is live, a key holder satisfies the gate without being a module at
;;            all, reaches DALOS core ops directly, and -- because IGNIS is collected in Talos and
;;            this route never enters it -- pays NOTHING.
;;METHOD:     call `DALOS::A_SetIgnisSourcePrice` straight at core, twice: once signed by an
;;            ordinary user, once by the master key. Measure the price AND the IGNIS charged.
;;RESULT:     CONFIRMED as measured -- the master key executed the op and was charged 0.0000 -- and
;;            then CORRECTED on review, which changed what the finding IS rather than whether it
;;            was real.
;;
;;ON THE STATUS FIELD: this reads FIXED, and it read SUCCEEDED when first measured. The field takes
;;one value and the honest one is the CURRENT state; the history is kept in full below, including
;;the part where this report described the finding more broadly than the evidence supported.
;;
;;THE CORRECTION, and it is the part worth publishing. The registration that produced this lives at
;;
;;    REPL/Stage_01/[2.1]_Dalos.repl        (a TEST FIXTURE)
;;
;;and NOWHERE else in the repository -- in particular, in no genesis payload. The DEPLOYED system
;;never had this exception. This block was reporting a live hole in CLAUDE.md's "only supported
;;client path" sentence; there was no hole. There was something else, and it is not obviously less
;;serious:
;;
;;    An audit harness that grants itself a privilege the real system withholds will certify
;;    behaviour nobody can reach.
;;
;;It was load-bearing, too. Five guard-type assertions in [2.1] called `ref-DALOS::C_Rotate*`
;;directly while being LABELLED with the Talos entrypoint names. They passed only because of this
;;registration, and removing it made them -- and only them, out of 21,732 assertions -- go red.
;;They now run through Talos at `[6.12]_DALOS-ADMIN.repl` <<TX-DA-004>>.
;;
;;FIXED 2026-09-14 on the owner's ruling: "master key passes as module is correct. RotateStoa must
;;pass through talos, if it doesn't it's a bug." The MECHANISM is correct and untouched -- a
;;registered module guard should satisfy `P|UEV_IMC`, and every real module still registers through
;;`P|A_AddIMP` at deploy. What is gone is the harness registering a KEY as though it were a module.
;;
;;WHAT THIS BLOCK ASSERTS NOW: the attack, re-run, and refused. The bound the original finding
;;established still holds and is still worth stating -- the same key could never operate the
;;collector against a third party, because `IGNIS::C_Collect` enforces the payer's own ownership.
;;*Skipping your own toll needs nobody else's signature; charging someone else's does.* The reachable
;;damage was unbilled ADMIN activity, never drained users. Now it is neither.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;an ordinary user cannot reach it -- the gate does work for everyone else.
            (expect-failure "<<RT-B-001>> an ordinary key cannot reach DALOS core: the gate holds for users"
                "None of the guards passed"
                (ref-DALOS::A_SetIgnisSourcePrice 0.5))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-B-001b - the master key tries the same gate, and is now turned away")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-B-001 · 02 · same call, master key, no Talos -- now REFUSED ====
(print "--- [RT-B-001 · 02 · same call, master key, no Talos -- now REFUSED] ---")
;;THE SAME ATTACK, RE-RUN AGAINST THE REPAIR. Before 2026-09-14 this block asserted three things
;;and all three passed: the OURO source price moved to 0.5, it genuinely changed, and the caller was
;;charged 0.0000 IGNIS. Those assertions are the reason this finding could be stated as a measured
;;fact rather than a suspicion, and they are what a green suite looked like WITH the hole open.
;;
;;They are inverted now. The master key is the most privileged signer in the system; it holds the
;;Demiurgoi keyset that governs every module. It still cannot reach a core `C_`/`A_` without being a
;;module, because being a module is not something a signature can be.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV2} TS01-A)
        (admin:string KST.ANHD)
    )
    (let
        (
            (price-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_OuroborosPrice))
            (ignis-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply admin false))
        )
        (map print
            [
                (format "<<RT-B-001>> OURO source price before = {}" [price-before])
                ;;1] THE REPAIR. Message-checked, so a refusal for an unrelated reason -- a missing
                ;;   signature, a keyset failure -- fails this assertion rather than passing it. That
                ;;   distinction has already changed a result twice in this programme.
                (expect-failure "<<RT-B-001>> the MASTER KEY can no longer reach DALOS core directly"
                    "None of the guards passed"
                    (ref-DALOS::A_SetIgnisSourcePrice 0.5))
                ;;2] RULE 9 discharge: refused before any write, so the price input is untouched.
                ;;   This is the assertion that says the admin did not half-execute.
                (expect "<<RT-B-001>> ...and the OURO source price was not moved"
                    price-before (ref-DALOS::UR_OuroborosPrice))
                ;;3] NON-VACUITY, and it is the half that makes the block mean something. A gate that
                ;;   refuses EVERYONE is not a boundary, it is an outage. The same admin operation,
                ;;   by the same signer, THROUGH TALOS, still works -- so what was removed is the
                ;;   unbilled shortcut, not the capability.
                (expect "<<RT-B-001>> ...while the admin's legitimate Talos route still works"
                    "Succesfuly set IGNIS price to 0.5"
                    (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_SetIgnisSourcePrice 0.5))
                (expect "<<RT-B-001>> ...and THAT route really moved the price"
                    0.5 (ref-DALOS::UR_OuroborosPrice))
            ]
        )
        ;;the IGNIS figure is printed rather than asserted: TS01-A admin wrappers are not IGNIS-billed
        ;;client ops, so "it now costs something" would be a false claim about the admin lane. What
        ;;the repair closed is the reach, not the price of admin work.
        (print (format "<<RT-B-001>> admin IGNIS delta across the Talos route = {}"
            [(- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply admin false))]))
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
;;rolled back: this moves a live price input, and leaving it moved would silently re-point every
;;downstream gas figure in the suite.
(rollback-tx)
